SDL3, SDL_ttf, SDL_mixer

https://www.libsdl.org/ says ...

Simple DirectMedia Layer is a cross-platform development library designed to provide low level access to audio, keyboard, mouse, joystick, and graphics hardware via OpenGL and Direct3D. It is used by video playback software, emulators, and popular games including Valve's award winning catalog and many Humble Bundle games.

SDL is distributed under the zlib license. This license allows you to use SDL freely in any software.

Google AI Overview ...

SDL3 officially supports Android and is designed to run on it, allowing for cross-platform development. It provides a dedicated Android project template in its source code to bridge C++ code with the Android Java frontend and supports compilation via Gradle and CMake

SDL_ttf and SDL_mixer are not part of the core SDL library (Simple DirectMedia Layer), but are official extension libraries (SDL_ttf, SDL_mixer). They are developed by the same team, maintain the same open-source license, and are designed to work alongside SDL to add font rendering (TTF) and audio mixing (Mixer) functionality

SDL3 is primarily developed in C and designed to work natively with C++, making them the top choices for building applications

ezApp includes some enhancements to the SDL3 
- capture device audio
- foreground mode
- text to speech
- location, lat,longitude, altitude MSL
- flashlight

